      "role": "user",
      "content": "{\"objective\":\"Prioritize evidence of compatibility across all three MSA conformers while weighing BOTH control conformers. A candidate with high MSA contacts and equally high control contacts provides weak discrimination evidence. Prefer repeatable compatible MSA poses; give control-compatible poses serious weight. pose_count=1 leaves repeatability unknown. A clashing control pose gives inconclusive control evidence, not proof of weak binding. A distorted peptide backbone makes a sampled pose physically unreliable; weigh peptide_cn_max_deviation_a. Distorted control peptides leave discrimination inconclusive. Strong contacts in distorted MSA poses provide weak support. Choose 24 sequences balancing evidence, sequence diversity, and epitope coverage. Describe uncertain candidates as exploratory. Every candidate now has two independent sampled poses per conformer in replicate_poses. Integrate both observations. Favor consistent MSA compatibility and attend to the strongest compatible control pose. Mark sampling-sensitive or target-distorting candidates exploratory. Rank all 24 finalists and cite replicate evidence.\",\"columns\":{\"chemistry\":[\"length\",\"gravy\",\"hydrophobic_run\"],\"conformer_metrics\":[\"contacts_per_residue\",\"clashes_per_residue\",\"assembly_clashes_per_residue\",\"polar_pairs_per_residue\",\"opposite_charge_pairs_per_residue\",\"repeat_contacts_range\",\"pose_count\",\"receptor_backbone_rmsd_a\",\"peptide_cn_max_deviation_a\"]},\"metrics\":{\"contacts_per_residue\":\"distinct peptide/receptor residue pairs within 4.5 A, normalized by peptide length\",\"clashes_per_residue\":\"heavy-atom pairs closer than 2 A / peptide length, central chain\",\"assembly_clashes_per_residue\":\"clashes against protein assembly / length, using relaxed modeled layers plus untouched other layers; compare geometry within each target\",\"receptor_backbone_rmsd_a\":\"C-alpha displacement of the three receptor layers from their experimental coordinates, no alignment; large displacement means the modeled target was distorted\",\"polar_pairs_per_residue\":\"N/O atom proximity <3.5 A / length, geometry proxy, hydrogen bonding needs angles\",\"opposite_charge_pairs_per_residue\":\"D/E vs K/R side-chain charged atom pairs <4.5 A / length\",\"repeat_contacts_range\":\"min/max across independently sampled poses; one pose initially, two for finalist audit\",\"contrast\":\"weakest MSA central-chain contact density minus strongest control contact density; geometric proxy\",\"gravy\":\"average hydrophobicity; larger often harder to dissolve\",\"peptide_cn_max_deviation_a\":\"maximum absolute deviation of consecutive-residue C-N distance from approximate ideal peptide bond length 1.33 A; large values indicate broken or severely distorted peptide geometry\",\"scope\":\"PepGLAD fixseq poses conditioned on homologous patches across three adjacent protein layers, restrained minimization with unlimited iterations and a specified force tolerance. Central-chain contacts are comparable geometry proxies. These are local hypotheses. Affinity and true selectivity await assays.\"},\"instructions\":\"Use supplied observations for ranking; mark unavailable evidence unknown. Assign every required candidate key a priority between 0 and 100; larger means earlier experimental priority. Use decimals to express meaningful distinctions and reserve equal values for genuine ties. Consider diversity and epitope coverage across the highest priorities. Priorities are contextual judgments, not binding probabilities. For replicated candidates, cite supplied numerical evidence briefly in support and limitation. Write decision_logic, support and limitation in plain Simplified Chinese for an AI researcher new to biology. Return concise JSON.\",\"candidates\":[{\"id\":\"C000\",\"site\":\"site_2\",\"sequence\":\"RYSNGSGNDVTRN\",\"chemistry\":[13,-1.785,1],\"conformers\":{\"6XYO\":[1.923,0.0,0.0,1.385,0.0,[1.923,1.923],1,0.255,0.045],\"6XYP\":[0.385,0.